# `npm --prefix <workspace>/tim link` (the install command in ../CLAUDE.md)
# treats tim/ as npm's global prefix, so it writes a bin/ shim and a
# lib/node_modules/ tree in here. The shim is a symlink into lib/, which is
# not tracked — so committing it leaves a dangling link in a fresh clone, and
# GitHub Actions aborts staging any composite action from this repo with
# "Could not find file '.../tim/bin/tim'". That silently unhooks every
# workflow that consumes DEFRA/trade-imports-workspace@main. The real entry
# point is the `bin` field in package.json; these are install residue.
bin/
lib/
